  "publishedAt": "2026-06-02T17:50:00.000Z",
  "content": "<div id=\"readability-page-1\" class=\"page\"><div> <p>From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia</p> </div><div lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\" id=\"mw-content-text\">\n\n<table><caption>Bay Model Visitor Center</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><span typeof=\"mw:File/Frameless\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:USCAE_Bay_Model_-_San_Francisco_Bay_Detail.jpg\"><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/USCAE_Bay_Model_-_San_Francisco_Bay_Detail.jpg/330px-USCAE_Bay_Model_-_San_Francisco_Bay_Detail.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"290\" height=\"218\" srcset=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/USCAE_Bay_Model_-_San_Francisco_Bay_Detail.jpg/960px-USCAE_Bay_Model_-_San_Francisco_Bay_Detail.jpg 2x\" data-file-width=\"3648\" data-file-height=\"2736\"></a></span><div><p>View of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Francisco_Bay\" title=\"San Francisco Bay\">San Francisco Bay</a> portion of the Bay Model.</p></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><div><div><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Location_Map_San_Francisco_Bay_Area.png\" title=\"U.S. Army Corps of Engineers Bay Model is located in San Francisco Bay Area\"><img alt=\"U.S. Army Corps of Engineers Bay Model is located in San Francisco Bay Area\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Location_Map_San_Francisco_Bay_Area.png/250px-Location_Map_San_Francisco_Bay_Area.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"250\" height=\"303\" srcset=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Location_Map_San_Francisco_Bay_Area.png/500px-Location_Map_San_Francisco_Bay_Area.png 2x\" data-file-width=\"524\" data-file-height=\"636\"></a></span></p><div><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><span title=\"U.S. Army Corps of Engineers Bay Model\"><img alt=\"U.S. Army Corps of Engineers Bay Model\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Red_pog.svg/20px-Red_pog.svg.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\" data-file-width=\"64\" data-file-height=\"64\"></span></span></p></div></div><p>Location within San Francisco Bay Area</p></div></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Established</th><td>1957</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Location</th><td>2100 Bridgeway, Sausalito, California</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Coordinates</th><td><span><span><a href=\"https://geohack.toolforge.org/geohack.php?pagename=U.S._Army_Corps_of_Engineers_Bay_Model&amp;params=37_51_48.61_N_122_29_41.75_W_type:landmark\"><span><span title=\"Maps, aerial photos, and other data for this location\"><span>37°51′48.61″N</span> <span>122°29′41.75″W</span></span></span><span>﻿ / ﻿</span><span><span title=\"Maps, aerial photos, and other data for this location\">37.8635028°N 122.4949306°W</span></span></a></span></span></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Key&nbsp;holdings</th><td>Hydraulic model of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Francisco_Bay\" title=\"San Francisco Bay\">San Francisco Bay</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sacramento%E2%80%93San_Joaquin_River_Delta\" title=\"Sacramento–San Joaquin River Delta\">Sacramento–San Joaquin River Delta</a></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Owners</th><td>US Army Corps of Engineers, San Francisco District</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\"><p>Public transit access</p></th><td><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Gate_Transit\" title=\"Golden Gate Transit\">Golden Gate Transit</a>, bus routes 2, 4, 30, or 92; or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Gate_Ferry\" title=\"Golden Gate Ferry\">Golden Gate Ferry</a> from San Francisco</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Website</th><td><span><span><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"http://www.spn.usace.army.mil/Missions/Recreation/Bay-Model-Visitor-Center/\">Official website</a></span></span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>The <b>U.S. Army Corps of Engineers Bay Model</b> is a working <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hydraulic\" title=\"Hydraulic\">hydraulic</a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scale_model\" title=\"Scale model\">scale model</a> of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Francisco_Bay\" title=\"San Francisco Bay\">San Francisco Bay</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sacramento-San_Joaquin_River_Delta\" title=\"Sacramento-San Joaquin River Delta\">Sacramento-San Joaquin River Delta</a> System.  While the Bay Model is still operational, it is no longer used for scientific research but is instead open to the public alongside educational exhibits about Bay hydrology. The model is located in the Bay Model Visitor Center at 2100 Bridgeway Blvd. in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sausalito,_California\" title=\"Sausalito, California\">Sausalito, California</a>.\n</p>\n<meta property=\"mw:PageProp/toc\">\n\n<p>In the late 1940s, John Reber proposed to build two large dams in the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Francisco_Bay\" title=\"San Francisco Bay\">San Francisco Bay</a> as a way to provide a more reliable freshwater supply to residents and farms and to connect local communities. In 1953, the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Army_Corps_of_Engineers\" title=\"U.S. Army Corps of Engineers\">U.S. Army Corps of Engineers</a> proposed a detailed study of the so-called <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reber_Plan\" title=\"Reber Plan\">Reber Plan</a>. Cornelius Biemond proposed a similar plan which would dam the Sacramento River in the delta region to feed aqueducts with freshwater. Authorized by Section 110 of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Rivers_and_Harbors_Act_of_1950&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"Rivers and Harbors Act of 1950 (page does not exist)\">Rivers and Harbors Act of 1950</a>, construction of the Bay Model was completed in 1957 to study the plans.<sup id=\"cite_ref-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\"><span>[</span>1<span>]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-2\"><span>[</span>2<span>]</span></a></sup> The tests proved that the plan was not viable, and the Reber Plan was scuttled.<sup id=\"cite_ref-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-3\"><span>[</span>3<span>]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>The <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sacramento-San_Joaquin_River_Delta\" title=\"Sacramento-San Joaquin River Delta\">Sacramento-San Joaquin River Delta</a> portion was added to the model in 1966-1969 to provide information for studies concerning impacts of the deepening of navigation channels, realignment of Delta channels (via the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peripheral_Canal\" title=\"Peripheral Canal\">Peripheral Canal</a>), and various flow arrangements on water quality. When completed, the expanded model covered 2 acres (0.81&nbsp;ha) of land.<sup id=\"cite_ref-4\"><a href=\"#cite_note-4\"><span>[</span>4<span>]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n\n<p>The model is approximately 320 feet long in the north-south direction and about 400 feet long in the east-west direction. It is constructed out of 286 five-ton <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Concrete\" title=\"Concrete\">concrete</a> slabs joined together like a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jigsaw_puzzle\" title=\"Jigsaw puzzle\">jigsaw puzzle</a>. Features that affect the water flow of the San Francisco Bay and Sacramento-San Joaquin Delta are reproduced, including <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ship_channel_(disambiguation)\" title=\"Ship channel (disambiguation)\">ship channels</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River\" title=\"River\">rivers</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stream\" title=\"Stream\">creeks</a>, sloughs, the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canal\" title=\"Canal\">canals</a> in the Delta, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cut_and_fill\" title=\"Cut and fill\">fills</a>, major <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wharf\" title=\"Wharf\">wharfs</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pier\" title=\"Pier\">piers</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slipway\" title=\"Slipway\">slips</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Levee\" title=\"Levee\">dikes</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bridge\" title=\"Bridge\">bridges</a>, and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breakwater_(structure)\" title=\"Breakwater (structure)\">breakwaters</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-autogenerated1_5-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-autogenerated1-5\"><span>[</span>5<span>]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>The limits of the model encompass the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pacific_Ocean\" title=\"Pacific Ocean\">Pacific Ocean</a> extending 17 miles beyond the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Gate\" title=\"Golden Gate\">Golden Gate</a>, San Francisco Bay, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Pablo_Bay\" title=\"San Pablo Bay\">San Pablo Bay</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suisun_Bay\" title=\"Suisun Bay\">Suisun Bay</a> and all of the Sacramento-San Joaquin River Delta to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Verona,_California\" title=\"Verona, California\">Verona</a>, 17 miles north of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sacramento,_California\" title=\"Sacramento, California\">Sacramento</a> on the north, and to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vernalis,_California\" title=\"Vernalis, California\">Vernalis</a>, 32 miles south of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stockton,_California\" title=\"Stockton, California\">Stockton</a> on the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Joaquin_River\" title=\"San Joaquin River\">San Joaquin River</a> on the south.<sup id=\"cite_ref-autogenerated1_5-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-autogenerated1-5\"><span>[</span>5<span>]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<div><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:USCAE_Bay_Model_-_San_Pablo_Bay_Panorama.jpg\" title=\"Panorama of the Bay Model focused on the area of the model representing the San Pablo Bay.\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/USCAE_Bay_Model_-_San_Pablo_Bay_Panorama.jpg/960px-USCAE_Bay_Model_-_San_Pablo_Bay_Panorama.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"376\" srcset=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/USCAE_Bay_Model_-_San_Pablo_Bay_Panorama.jpg/1920px-USCAE_Bay_Model_-_San_Pablo_Bay_Panorama.jpg 2x\" data-file-width=\"7390\" data-file-height=\"3473\"></a></span></p><div><p>Panorama of the Bay Model focused on the area of the model representing the San Pablo Bay.</p></div></div> <p>The scale of the model is 1:1000 on the horizontal axis and 1:100 on the vertical axis. The model operates at a time scale of 1:100.<sup id=\"cite_ref-autogenerated2_6-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-autogenerated2-6\"><span>[</span>6<span>]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>The model is distorted by a factor of ten between the horizontal and vertical scales. The distortion is designed into the model to ensure a proper hydraulic flow over the tidal flats and shallows. The distortion does increase the hydraulic efficiency of the flows. These increased efficiencies are corrected by the use of copper strips throughout the model. The exact number of copper strips is adjusted during the calibration of the model.<sup id=\"cite_ref-autogenerated2_6-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-autogenerated2-6\"><span>[</span>6<span>]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n\n<div><ol>\n<li id=\"cite_note-1\"><span><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-1\">^</a></b></span> <span><cite id=\"CITEREFHunt2012\">Hunt, Mary Ellen (July 18, 2012). <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"http://www.sfgate.com/default/article/San-Francisco-Bay-Model-Sausalito-3717931.php\">\"San Francisco Bay Model, Sausalito\"</a>. <i>SFGate.com</i><span>. Retrieved <span>October 20,</span> 2012</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=SFGate.com&amp;rft.atitle=San+Francisco+Bay+Model%2C+Sausalito&amp;rft.date=2012-07-18&amp;rft.aulast=Hunt&amp;rft.aufirst=Mary+Ellen&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.sfgate.com%2Fdefault%2Farticle%2FSan-Francisco-Bay-Model-Sausalito-3717931.php&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AU.S.+Army+Corps+of+Engineers+Bay+Model\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-2\"><span><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-2\">^</a></b></span> <span><cite><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=zgcrAAAAIBAJ&amp;sjid=eZgFAAAAIBAJ&amp;pg=4647%2C4594376\">\"Model Bay Is Studied\"</a>. <i>Reading Eagle</i>. U.P. July 14, 1957<span>. Retrieved <span>August 18,</span> 2016</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Reading+Eagle&amp;rft.atitle=Model+Bay+Is+Studied&amp;rft.date=1957-07-14&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fnews.google.com%2Fnewspapers%3Fid%3DzgcrAAAAIBAJ%26sjid%3DeZgFAAAAIBAJ%26pg%3D4647%252C4594376&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AU.S.+Army+Corps+of+Engineers+Bay+Model\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-3\"><span><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-3\">^</a></b></span> <span><cite id=\"CITEREFJordan2009\">Jordan, Dick (August 2, 2009). <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"http://www.batw.org/articles/dick-jordan_bay-model_dec-2010/\">\"Water Lab Lets Visitors Peek Beneath the Bay\"</a>. <i>Bay Area Newsgroup</i><span>. Retrieved <span>October 20,</span> 2012</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Bay+Area+Newsgroup&amp;rft.atitle=Water+Lab+Lets+Visitors+Peek+Beneath+the+Bay&amp;rft.date=2009-08-02&amp;rft.aulast=Jordan&amp;rft.aufirst=Dick&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.batw.org%2Farticles%2Fdick-jordan_bay-model_dec-2010%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AU.S.+Army+Corps+of+Engineers+Bay+Model\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-4\"><span><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-4\">^</a></b></span> <span><cite><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=ZRw_AAAAIBAJ&amp;sjid=Qk8MAAAAIBAJ&amp;pg=7335%2C6376994\">\"Bay Model's Dedication Scheduled For Saturday\"</a>. <i>Lodi News-Sentinel</i>. June 12, 1969<span>. Retrieved <span>August 18,</span> 2016</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Lodi+News-Sentinel&amp;rft.atitle=Bay+Model%27s+Dedication+Scheduled+For+Saturday&amp;rft.date=1969-06-12&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fnews.google.com%2Fnewspapers%3Fid%3DZRw_AAAAIBAJ%26sjid%3DQk8MAAAAIBAJ%26pg%3D7335%252C6376994&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AU.S.+Army+Corps+of+Engineers+Bay+Model\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-autogenerated1-5\"><span>^ <a href=\"#cite_ref-autogenerated1_5-0\"><sup><i><b>a</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-autogenerated1_5-1\"><sup><i><b>b</b></i></sup></a></span> <span><cite><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"http://www.spn.usace.army.mil/Missions/Recreation/Bay-Model-Visitor-Center/The-Bay-Model-Journey/History/\">\"History of the Bay Model\"</a>. US Army Corps of Engineers<span>. Retrieved <span>August 18,</span> 2016</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=History+of+the+Bay+Model&amp;rft.pub=US+Army+Corps+of+Engineers&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.spn.usace.army.mil%2FMissions%2FRecreation%2FBay-Model-Visitor-Center%2FThe-Bay-Model-Journey%2FHistory%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AU.S.+Army+Corps+of+Engineers+Bay+Model\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-autogenerated2-6\"><span>^ <a href=\"#cite_ref-autogenerated2_6-0\"><sup><i><b>a</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-autogenerated2_6-1\"><sup><i><b>b</b></i></sup></a></span> <span><cite><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.spn.usace.army.mil/Missions/Recreation/Bay-Model-Visitor-Center/The-Bay-Model-Journey/Technical-Side/\">\"The Technical Side of the Bay Model\"</a>. US Army Corps of Engineers<span>. Retrieved <span>August 18,</span> 2016</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=The+Technical+Side+of+the+Bay+Model&amp;rft.pub=US+Army+Corps+of+Engineers&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.spn.usace.army.mil%2FMissions%2FRecreation%2FBay-Model-Visitor-Center%2FThe-Bay-Model-Journey%2FTechnical-Side%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AU.S.+Army+Corps+of+Engineers+Bay+Model\"></span></span>\n</li>\n</ol></div> <ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.spn.usace.army.mil/Missions/Recreation/Bay-Model-Visitor-Center/\">Bay Model Visitor Center</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XhlhykM_puk\"><span>A Visit to the US Army Corps of Engineers \"Bay Model\"</span></a> on <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/YouTube_video_(identifier)\" title=\"YouTube video (identifier)\">YouTube</a></li>\n<li><cite><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=ruUzAAAAIBAJ&amp;sjid=t-4HAAAAIBAJ&amp;pg=3763%2C5416080\">\"Army Scale Model Seen By Mayor\"</a>. <i>Lodi News-Sentinel</i>. June 14, 1957<span>. Retrieved <span>August 18,</span> 2016</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Lodi+News-Sentinel&amp;rft.atitle=Army+Scale+Model+Seen+By+Mayor&amp;rft.date=1957-06-14&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fnews.google.com%2Fnewspapers%3Fid%3DruUzAAAAIBAJ%26sjid%3Dt-4HAAAAIBAJ%26pg%3D3763%252C5416080&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AU.S.+Army+Corps+of+Engineers+Bay+Model\"></span></li>\n<li><cite><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=eQFOAAAAIBAJ&amp;sjid=E4wDAAAAIBAJ&amp;pg=5410%2C1060781\">\"Little Chesapeake\"</a>. <i>The Free Lance-Star</i>. July 8, 1978<span>. Retrieved <span>August 18,</span> 2016</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Free+Lance-Star&amp;rft.atitle=Little+Chesapeake&amp;rft.date=1978-07-08&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fnews.google.com%2Fnewspapers%3Fid%3DeQFOAAAAIBAJ%26sjid%3DE4wDAAAAIBAJ%26pg%3D5410%252C1060781&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AU.S.+Army+Corps+of+Engineers+Bay+Model\"></span> A larger model of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chesapeake_Bay\" title=\"Chesapeake Bay\">Chesapeake Bay</a> also built (1976) by the USACE.</li></ul>\n\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nParsed by mw‐web.eqiad.main‐6987bbd4f6‐7bw7j\nCached time: 20260603165444\nCache expiry: 2592000\nCache expiry source: Module:Citation/CS1 (os.date(%Y))\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [vary‐revision‐sha1, prevent‐selective‐update, show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.746 seconds\nReal time usage: 1.116 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 1800/1000000\nRevision size: 8227/2097152 bytes\nPost‐expand include size: 79086/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 5598/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 18/100\nExpensive parser function count: 3/500\nUnstrip recursion depth: 1/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 43030/5000000 bytes\nLua time usage: 0.448/10.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 10209113/52428800 bytes\nNumber of Wikibase entities loaded: 1/500\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%  966.463 1 -total\n 23.24%  224.644 1 Template:Infobox_museum\n 21.66%  209.290 1 Template:Infobox\n 18.15%  175.437 1 Template:Reflist\n 16.73%  161.737 1 Template:San_Francisco_Bay_watershed\n 16.03%  154.960 1 Template:Navbox\n 15.94%  154.102 6 Template:Cite_news\n 14.77%  142.779 1 Template:Short_description\n 10.71%  103.509 1 Template:Commons_category\n 10.38%  100.334 1 Template:Sister_project\n-->\n\n<!-- Render ID eba8a93a-5f6c-11f1-b7c1-6b57975b4ed8 -->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key enwiki:pcache:25016032:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20260603165444 and revision id 1356103442. Rendering was triggered because: page_view\n -->\n</d